# Deny the entire workspace unless the Dockerfile needs it explicitly.
**

# Dependency manifests and build configuration.
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!tsconfig.json
!vite.config.ts
!index.html

# Runtime entry point and source trees. Parent directory exceptions are
# intentional: Docker must traverse them before the recursive rules apply.
!server.ts
!server/
!server/**
!src/
!src/**
!public/
!public/**

# WHY THIS MODULE SITS AT THE REPOSITORY ROOT AND NOT IN scripts/.
#
# `vite.config.ts` imports `./vite-cache-dir.mjs` (it decides where Vite's
# dependency-optimizer cache goes, which cannot be `node_modules/.vite` — see
# that file's header), so the builder stage's `npm run build` cannot resolve
# the config without it. `Dockerfile:13-14` is `COPY . .` + `RUN npm run
# build`, and release.yml / edge.yml build with `context: .`, so this file is
# what decides whether that succeeds.
#
# The module lived at `scripts/lib/vite-cache-dir.mjs` first, and allowlisting
# it there does not work narrowly. Under the ordered Moby semantics this
# policy uses — and which `tests/core/docker-context.test.ts` models — a
# pattern may match a path OR A PARENT, so the `!scripts/` traversal exception
# that Docker needs before it will descend at all ALSO un-denies every other file
# under `scripts/`. Measured with that model: with
# `!scripts/`, `!scripts/lib/`, `!scripts/lib/vite-cache-dir.mjs` in place,
# `scripts/honesty-audit.mjs` and `scripts/verify-vite-cache-isolation.mjs`
# both come back NOT excluded. Getting back to one file needs a re-deny/
# re-allow sequence whose correctness depends on pattern order and on which
# rules happen to match directories rather than files — a rule that works
# today and rots silently.
#
# At the root it is one line, with no parent to traverse and no subtree to
# re-deny, and it sits beside the `vite.config.ts` it configures. `scripts/`
# stays fully denied: it is maintainer tooling (browser gates, corpus
# measurement, the rulebook generator, the honesty audit) and none of it is a
# build input.
!vite-cache-dir.mjs

# Defense in depth for confidential, generated, and runtime state. These
# remain excluded even if a future allow rule is added above.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
/data
/data/**
.git
.git/**
**/.git
**/.git/**
node_modules
node_modules/**
**/node_modules
**/node_modules/**
*.db
**/*.db
*.db-wal
**/*.db-wal
*.db-shm
**/*.db-shm
*.log
**/*.log
dist
dist/**
coverage
coverage/**
docs
docs/**
tests
tests/**
